{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The gate mechanics are now reproducible: each colored control couples an external crossbar to one arm of the central four-way mechanism. The chamber has a single bottom opening, so the reusable operation is to rotate a chosen central arm to that opening, extend it to gain clearance, slide the linked crossbar around the fixed peg, retract, then rotate the terminal arm into the same opening. I’m testing that staged macro directly against marker depth."}}
